 "notes": "ALP-photon exclusion (Fig. 13, June 2013 run in 3 T magnet, 95% CL) extracted from the vector path of the CROWS region in the e-print file ALP_excl_plot.pdf. Boundary matches quoted values: most sensitive g=4.5e-8 GeV^-1 at ma=7.2 ueV (extracted 4.52e-8 at 7.196e-6 eV) and wideband plateau g=9.9e-8 GeV^-1 (extracted 9.85e-8). Flat plateau extends to the plot's left edge; first point clamped to ma=1e-12 eV. Curve ends where the boundary reaches the top of the plotted range (g~0.8 GeV^-1 at ma~2.9e-4 eV). Microwave LSW experiment: no dark-matter density assumption. Paper also sets a hidden-sector-photon kinetic-mixing limit (Fig. 14), not reported here; the ALP g limit is the axion-photon coupling in the standard aFFdual normalisation used for comparison with ALPS-I and CAST.",
